window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-6afd18fb00f3b1ba"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"write-vulnerability-reports\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">编写漏洞报告</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>使用 <code>$codex-security:vulnerability-writeup</code>，为每个不同的漏洞编写一份自包含的报告。你可以从 Codex Security 扫描结果开始，也可以直接使用提供的发现项、披露说明、概念验证（PoC）和源代码。不要求必须先运行 Codex Security 扫描。</p> <p><a id=\"prepare-the-evidence\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">准备证据</h2> <p>向工作流提供：</p> <ul> <li>需要审查的发现项、披露说明或评估文档。</li> <li>目标源代码树，以及受影响的修订版本或发布版本。</li> <li>已有的 PoC、日志、跟踪记录、屏幕截图或诊断输出。</li> <li>可用时，提供修复提交或差异（diff）。</li> </ul> <p>Codex 会在撰写报告前，依据受影响的源代码核实每项陈述。如果无法取得源代码或受影响的修订版本，请先决定是否要继续生成报告，并明确标出未经验证的陈述。</p> <p><a id=\"run-the-workflow\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">运行工作流</h2> <p>发送类似下面的提示：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:vulnerability-writeup to create one self-contained report for each distinct vulnerability in [input paths]. Verify the claims against [source path and revision], preserve or improve the supplied PoCs, and write the reports to [output directory]. Use a local test environment for reproductions.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请使用 $codex-security:vulnerability-writeup，为 [input paths] 中每个不同的漏洞创建一份独立完整的报告。对照 [source path and revision] 验证相关主张，保留或改进所提供的 PoC，并将报告写入 [output directory]。复现时使用本地测试环境。</div></div> <p>Codex 会清点所提供的材料，将描述相同根本原因和易受攻击路径的报告归为一组，并为每个不同的漏洞创建一个报告目录。每个目录都包含一份 Markdown 报告；如果提供了支持 PoC 的文件，还会包含一个 <code>poc/</code> 目录。</p> <p><a id=\"review-each-report\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">审阅每份报告</h2> <p>分发报告前，请确认报告：</p> <ul> <li>从攻击者可控的入口一路追踪到被破坏的安全不变量和实际影响。</li> <li>区分已验证的行为、假设和仍未解决的限制。</li> <li>引用源代码片段，并注明路径、函数和受影响的修订版本。</li> <li>在 PoC 可行时，包含 PoC 源码、构建或运行说明、代表性输出和安全限制。</li> <li>使用可移植的路径，不依赖内部存储位置或本机绝对路径。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"use-reports-from-a-scan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">使用扫描生成的报告</h2> <p>标准扫描、深度扫描和变更扫描都可以选择生成详细漏洞报告，并非必须生成。启用后，Codex 会将每份报告写入 <code>findings/&lt;slug&gt;/&lt;slug&gt;.md</code>，将支持文件放在 <code>findings/&lt;slug&gt;/poc/</code> 下，并在 <code>report.md</code> 中链接到报告。</p> <p>分享或归档扫描结果时，请将完整扫描目录放在一起。若要寻找能够解决多份报告中共同模式的改进方案，请继续阅读<a href=\"#/article/a-24294757e701b587\">提出安全加固方案</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"write-vulnerability-reports\">Write vulnerability reports</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use <code>$codex-security:vulnerability-writeup</code> to create a self-contained report for each distinct vulnerability. You can start from Codex Security scan results or use supplied findings, disclosure notes, PoCs, and source code directly. A Codex Security scan isn't required.</p> <h2 id=\"prepare-the-evidence\">Prepare the evidence</h2> <p>Provide the workflow with:</p> <ul> <li>The findings, disclosure notes, or assessment documents to review.</li> <li>The target source tree and affected revision or release.</li> <li>Existing PoCs, logs, traces, screenshots, or diagnostic output.</li> <li>Fix commits or diffs when available.</li> </ul> <p>Codex checks each claim against the affected source code before writing the report. If the source or affected revision isn't available, decide whether to proceed with a report that identifies the unverified claims.</p> <h2 id=\"run-the-workflow\">Run the workflow</h2> <p>Send a prompt like:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $codex-security:vulnerability-writeup to create one self-contained report for each distinct vulnerability in [input paths]. Verify the claims against [source path and revision], preserve or improve the supplied PoCs, and write the reports to [output directory]. Use a local test environment for reproductions.\n</code></pre> <p>Codex inventories the supplied material, groups reports that describe the same root cause and vulnerable path, and creates one report directory per distinct vulnerability. Each directory contains a Markdown report and a <code>poc/</code> directory when supporting PoC files are available.</p> <h2 id=\"review-each-report\">Review each report</h2> <p>Before distributing a report, confirm that it:</p> <ul> <li>Traces the bug from the attacker-controlled entry point to the broken security invariant and impact.</li> <li>Distinguishes verified behavior from hypotheses and unresolved constraints.</li> <li>Includes source excerpts with paths, functions, and the affected revision.</li> <li>Includes PoC source, build or run instructions, representative output, and safety limitations when a PoC is practical.</li> <li>Uses portable paths and doesn't depend on internal storage or local absolute paths.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"use-reports-from-a-scan\">Use reports from a scan</h2> <p>Detailed vulnerability reports are optional for standard, deep, and change scans. When you request them, Codex writes each report to <code>findings/&lt;slug&gt;/&lt;slug&gt;.md</code>, stores supporting files under <code>findings/&lt;slug&gt;/poc/</code>, and links the report from <code>report.md</code>.</p> <p>Keep the complete scan directory together when sharing or archiving a scan. To look for improvements that address patterns across the reports, continue with <a href=\"#/article/a-24294757e701b587\">Propose security hardening</a>.</p>"};
